From faa1a105860144fe1ea5b91c85f2ff6551dbc45d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduard Ralph <eduard@ralphovi.net>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 13:07:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Delete RebuildTypes addon per author's request

`RebuildTypes/RebuildTypes.gpr.py` declares
`include_in_listing=False`, `status=UNSTABLE`, `category=TOOL_DBFIX`
and `authors=["Nick Hall"]` - it is not published to users and is
flagged as a database-modifying tool that may corrupt data. The
addon also carried two stale Gramps-3 era pre-namespace imports
(`from gui.plug import tool`, `from QuestionDialog import OkDialog`)
that broke plugin registration on Python 3, so a load-time fix
would have been needed to revive it.

On PR https://github.com/gramps-project/addons-source/pull/877
(closed 2026-05-15, the prior port attempt) the addon's author and
the project maintainer agreed to drop it rather than port:

  Nick-Hall: "The RebuildTypes addon was either just an example or
  written for a particular person to fix a bug. An export followed
  by an import will achieve the same result. The Type Cleanup tool
  may also be a better option. I am happy for this addon to be
  deleted."

  GaryGriffin: "Seeing TOOL_DBFIX and UNSTABLE together is scary
  for a released addon."

Replace the dead/dangerous addon with its absence. Users needing
the same outcome have two supported alternatives Nick named:

  - export / re-import (rebuilds the type catalogue as a side
    effect of the round-trip)
  - the Type Cleanup tool (which is published and maintained)

No listing impact - the addon was already `include_in_listing=False`,
so `addons/gramps*/listings/addons-*.json` did not reference it; no
other tree references it either (`grep -rn RebuildTypes` on
`upstream/maintenance/gramps60` returns hits only inside the
`RebuildTypes/` directory itself).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
